The proposed retroactive application of strict 'Deliverability' and 'Hourly Matching' criteria could create significant financial reporting risks under IFRS/GAAP:
• IAS 37 : existing long-term PPAs (10-15 years) signed at a premium specifically for Scope 2 claims may become 'onerous' if they no longer qualify under the new rules. The unavoidable costs of the contract would exceed the economic benefits (as the 'green' value is nullified for reporting), potentially requiring immediate provision recognition on the balance sheet;
• IFRS 9: strict deliverability boundaries may sever the link between the generation asset and the consumption site. This could disqualify contracts from the 'own-use' exemption, forcing us to treat long-term energy contracts as financial derivatives measured at fair value through profit or loss (FVTPL), introducing significant artificial volatility to the P&L.
